  "body": {
    "id": "lem:balanced-wsvd-certificate",
    "kind": "lemma",
    "statement": "Under the balanced rank-one one-chart assumptions, for all sufficiently large even \\(n\\), the total algorithm \\(\\mathsf{WSVD}_n\\) is randomized polynomial-time and \\[(\\widehat L_n,\\widehat R_{\\alpha,n})\\in\\mathcal H_{\\alpha,n},\\qquad \\sup_{\\vartheta_n\\in\\Theta_n}\\mathbb E_{\\mathbb Q_{\\vartheta,n},\\Xi_n,\\Zeta_n}[\\widehat R_{\\alpha,n}]\\le C\\sigma\\sqrt n,\\] where \\(C\\) depends only on \\(\\alpha,\\mu,\\kappa,s_-,s_+\\). Honesty includes every singular or failed-stability sample through the deterministic fallback, and the expected-radius assertion follows by adding the separately controlled conditional Gaussian, simulation, homogeneous Taylor, and fallback terms in Lemma \\ref{lem:balanced-radius-audit}.",
    "free_symbols": [
